the requirement clearly specifies the four cases and HTTP status codes.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to handle the 409 case when trying to confirm a non-CREATED shipment (will only occur if CANCELLED, since CONFIRMED retries succeed silently).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if shipment doesn't exist\n   - Throws `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` if shipment is CANCELLED\n   - If shipment is CREATED, updates to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If shipment is already CONFIRMED, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns the (possibly unchanged) shipment as `ResponseEntity.ok()`\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test methods covering:\n   - Confirm a CREATED shipment → moves to CONFIRMED, returns 200\n   - Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → succeeds, changes nothing, returns 200\n   - Confirm a CANCELLED shipment → fails with 409 and `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` code\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment → fails with 404 and `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` code\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Scenario | Input | Repository operation | Status | Response |\n|----------|-------|----------------------|--------|----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById, save (modified) | 200 | Shipment with CONFIRMED status |\n| CONFIRMED (retry) | shipmentId | findById | 200 | Shipment unchanged, CONFIRMED status |\n| CANCELLED conflict | shipmentId | findById | 409 | `{error: {code: SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS, message: \"...\"}}` |\n| Not found | shipmentId | findById | 404 | `{error: {code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message: \"...\"}}` |\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nCould have added a separate `confirmShipment()` method in the repository layer, but the ticket says not to modify files outside the shipment feature except tests. Since the repository is part of the shipment feature, adding such a method would be over-engineering - the controller can handle the simple state transition directly (find, check status, update, save).\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1: POST confirm on CREATED → expect 200, shipment with CONFIRMED status\n- Test 2: POST confirm on already CONFIRMED → expect 200, no status change\n- Test 3: POST confirm on CANCELLED → expect 409, error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n- Test 4: POST confirm with unknown shipmentId → expect 404, error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. First, I'll add the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_read_input_tokens":15616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79148dae-5314-4179-939e-88ade1933876","uuid":"8e71bc7a-9eb8-4af0-b5b5-d18913ec9fe3","timestamp":"2026-09-09T08:08:46.967Z","request_id":"req_011CesXLTPrvhxYXNykfLS7C"}
